From: pkgdemon <pkgdemonteam@gmail.com>
Subject: NextBSD: udev_monitor on IOKit notifications instead of devd
Origin: NextBSD, nextbsd/nextbsd-displayserver-support#2
Forwarded: not-needed

NextBSD has no devd. Replace the monitor's devd reader thread with IOKit
first-match and terminated notifications on IOHIDDevice entries
(udev_iokit_watch, previous patch), delivered on a private serial
dispatch queue. Each event is queued as (syspath, action) and one byte is
written to the monitor's pipe, whose read end stays the pollable monitor
fd; udev_monitor_receive_device() builds the device and applies the
filters on the caller's thread. Removal is reported with the syspath the
add used (registry id -> syspath cache); entries present when the
monitor starts are remembered, not reported. The watch starts only for
monitors that can take "input" devices. No devd socket is opened.

--- a/udev-filter.c
+++ b/udev-filter.c
@@ -258,4 +258,22 @@
 
 	/* Not empty, matched nothing */
 	return false;
+}
+
+/*
+ * NextBSD: could a device of @p subsystem pass these filters? True when no
+ * positive subsystem filter is set (only tags, properties, ...), else as
+ * udev_filter_match_subsystem(). Used to start the IOKit input watch only
+ * for monitors that can receive input devices.
+ */
+bool
+udev_filter_wants_subsystem(struct udev_filter_head *ufh, const char *subsystem)
+{
+	struct udev_filter_entry *ufe;
+
+	STAILQ_FOREACH(ufe, ufh, next) {
+		if (ufe->type == UDEV_FILTER_TYPE_SUBSYSTEM && ufe->neg == 0)
+			return (udev_filter_match_subsystem(ufh, subsystem));
+	}
+	return (true);
 }
