+/*
+ * NextBSD: the monitor follows IOHIDDevice entries in the IORegistry
+ * (udev-iokit.c) instead of reading devd's socket; NextBSD has no devd.
+ *
+ * Same shape as libudev-devd's: a pipe whose read end is the monitor fd
+ * (pollable with poll, kqueue or epoll-shim, which is what libinput and the
+ * X server need) and a producer that queues one event and writes one byte
+ * per hotplug. The producer is libIOKit's notification callback on a
+ * private serial dispatch queue rather than a devd reader thread. It
+ * queues only a syspath and an action; the udev_device is built, and the
+ * monitor's filters applied, in udev_monitor_receive_device() on the
+ * caller's thread, so no libudev object is touched off that thread.
+ *
+ * Only input nodes have hotplug events. DRM connector hotplug needs an
+ * IOKit interest notification first (nextbsd-kernel#338); until then a
+ * monitor for "drm" alone is never readable, as before.
+ */
+
